From d2959ccea19612a6ef23e37c539bc6095618b688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:21:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: tell a TV input without Dolby Vision from an
 EDID read in part

Hades: where the display information has no Dolby Vision block at all, the
player information said "this TV input has no Dolby Vision Standard", the words
for a block without the Standard mode too, and the log "the display does not
advertise Dolby Vision Standard". A TV input in its 4K120/VRR mode (a Sony Bravia
8 II on "Enhanced format (Advanced)", hadesdevls/LibreELEC-Hades#7) left its user
unable to tell whether the TV offers no Dolby Vision there or Hades did not read
it.

DV_DISPLAY::Reason() now gives, where the EDID has no Dolby Vision block:
- nodv, for an EDID read whole: "this TV input offers no Dolby Vision";
- edidpart, where blocks that the EDID counts are missing or a block repeats
  block 0 (CDisplayInfo::EdidMissingBlocks(), BaseBlockCopy()): "the TV's EDID
  was read only in part", with the Display row "unknown: EDID read in part",
  since the block may be in what is missing.
"display" stays for a Dolby Vision block without a mode that native output
sends, and for no display information; invalid, legacy and lloff are as they
were. The Display row comes from DV_DISPLAY::DisplayState(), which is what
CWinSystemGbm::DisplayDolbyVisionSupport() did, with "part" added. The line of the
log with the shape of the EDID is now written for every reason that the EDID
decides (DV_DISPLAY::LogsEdidShape(): lloff, legacy, nodv and edidpart too, not
only display and invalid), once for each EDID. The two new reasons are of the
TV input on the overview page (PLAYERINFO::TodoForReason()).

Checked on the host with xbmc/utils/DisplayInfo.cpp built whole with
libdisplay-info 0.4.0, on a matrix of 16 EDIDs and on 1174 EDIDs: the only
reasons that change are "display" of an EDID without any Dolby block (21 become
nodv, 292 edidpart: those with blocks missing or a copy of block 0), and the
Display row of those 292.

Strings 41170 to 41172 of Estuary, in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx.
